  "question": {
    "text": "Consider the following diagram in which an inextensible string connects two blocks passing via ring. The first block moves with a velocity of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>and the second one moves with a velocity of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>.&nbsp;If the ring slides on horizontal rod then the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math> is (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/WhatsApp_Image_2020-07-04_at_1.31.52_PM.jpeg\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 125px;\" />",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "TrqTR",
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
